up", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "payments-api-v5.1.0-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55951, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01RCGQpbdBSMHSgtj4aC51sQ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 57442, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_012LZCAEJKdXaR9dfLxV65j3", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "payments-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 57742, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_012LZCAEJKdXaR9dfLxV65j3", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57742, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012LZCAEJKdXaR9dfLxV65j3", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 62568, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments back to its last healthy release and opened the SEV2. The error rate is back to normal.\n\n- **Service:** No service is called just \"payments\". The affected one is **payments-api**. This morning's release, v5.1.0, was running in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) and was unhealthy, with an error rate of about 18%.\n- **Rollback:** I moved payments-api back to **v5.0.0** in all production regions. Its release history shows it as the most recent version that was healthy in production. It no longer has a \"Rolled out\" status. Because v5.0.0 was healthy before, this didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **Check:** After the rollback the service reports healthy, with an error rate of about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2, payments-api), which paged on-call. It notes that someone needs to find the root cause in v5.1.0 before it's deployed again.", "error": nul